# DRY without premature abstraction

- One owning implementation. Other callers import or invoke it.
- Extract only at the second real use.
- No generic `utils/`, `helpers/`, or `common/` junk drawer.
- Environment differences are data (mani / sake / tofu vars), not a copied tree.
- Workspaces may share a contract. Do not copy source across remotes.
- Do not copy files across independent remotes to "share" code — share a contract.
